<%#
  /offline — FR-30's fallback page, precached by the service worker at install.

  It is deliberately plain: the visitor may be on a 3G bar with no data left,
  and everything else they need is already in their cache. The rule for the
  copy is the project's usual one — say what is true rather than what sounds
  reassuring. "You are offline" is true; "please check your connection" blames
  the visitor for our inability to fetch.
%>
<section class="section offline">
  <div class="container offline__inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">Offline</p>
    <h1>You are offline, and this page is on your device</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      HonestCars keeps working without a connection for the pages you have already opened here —
      the listings you looked at, anything you saved, and the apps shell around them.
    </p>

    <div class="offline__grid">
      <div class="offline__card">
        <h2>Already saved on this device</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Pages you have opened, including car pages you read</li>
          <li>Anything you saved to your shortlist</li>
          <li>Enquiries you typed: they wait on the device and send themselves the moment you are back online</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="offline__card">
        <h2>Needs a connection</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Pages you have never opened on this device</li>
          <li>Fresh prices, new stock and inspection reports</li>
          <li>Sending an enquiry, paying, or signing in</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="offline__note">
      Nothing you typed has been lost. An enquiry that could not be sent is held on this device and
      sent as soon as the phone is back on a network.
    </p>

    <div class="offline__actions">
      <button class="btn btn--primary" type="button" data-offline-retry>Try again</button>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/cars">Back to cars</a>
    </div>

    <p class="offline__small">
      If the button does nothing, the phone is still off the network — the pages that are already
      saved here keep working either way.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
